kipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... the Bardo, which won the 2017 Man Booker Prize for best work of fiction in English, and was a finalist for the Golden Man Booker, in which one Booker winner was selected to represent each decade, from the fifty years since the Prize's inception.\\n\\nHis stories have ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"}],\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize winners list 2016 2017 2018 2019\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d12\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sellout | Satire | |\\n| 2017 | George Saunders | Lincoln in the Bardo | Historical/experimental novel | |\\n| 2018 | Anna Burns | Milkman | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Margaret Atwood | The Testaments | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Bernardine Evaristo The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-09-26 |website=thebookerprizes.com |date=28 May 1959 |language=en}} | Girl, Woman ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... translated into) the English language.\\n\\nThere have been three special awards celebrating the Booker's history. In 1993, the \\\"Booker of Bookers\\\" prize was awarded to Salman Rushdie for Midnight's Children (the 1981 winner) as the best novel to win the award in its first 25 years ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d33\",\"snippet\":\" ... Importantly, however, this opening up of the canon and reliance on prizes as a tool to promote multiculturalism belies substantial inequalities along racial lines in global English-language book publishing (Childress 2017; Childress and Nault 2019; Chong 2011; McGrath 2019; Saha and van Lente 2022; So 2020). Because ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2019\\n\\nNo major changes for the press, but another good year for prize attention. Amy Arnold's Slip of a Fish landed a 2019 Goldsmiths Prize shortlisting, while Alia Trabucco Zerán's The Remainder was shortlisted for the Man Booker International Prize. Multiple translation prize wins and shortlistings ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"}],\"query\":\"International Booker Prize shortlist 2017 2018 2019 translated 25 languages\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_39ee29d3cba8465ebdc569d9"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2018, the Polish novelist was recognized for \\\"Flights,\\\" which she calls a \\\"constellation novel,\\\" owing to its fragmentary form and genre-defying style, and which won that year's Man Booker Prize. \\\"Drive Your Plow Over the Bones of the Dead,\\\" her latest novel to be translated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2019-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d52\",\"snippet\":\" ... the most significant young publishers of translated fiction is Jacques Testard's Fitzcarraldo Editions, which since its inception in 2014 has published one International Booker prize winner (Olga Tokarczuk's Flights, translated by Jennifer Croft) and three Nobel literature laureates: Tokarczuk, Annie Ernaux and Svetlana Alexievich.\\n\\nSo what ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/29/its-exciting-its-powerful-how-translated-fiction-captured-a-new-generation-of-readers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... Daisy Rockwell | Hindi | India | Tilted Axis Press |\\n\\n| The Books of Jacob | Olga Tokarczuk | Jennifer Croft | Polish | Poland | Fitzcarraldo Editions |\\n\\nAs you'll recall, Wynne is the first International Booker Prize jury chair who is a translator. He was joined on the panel by:\\n\\n- Author and academic Merve Emre ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... Olga Tokarczuk was a Finalist for Translated Literature in 2018 and Longlisted in 2019. The authors and translators on the list have been recognized by numerous international prizes, including the Akutagawa Prize, the Prix de la Littérature Arabe, the International Booker Prize, and the PEN Translation Prize. Their ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nationalbook.org/2022-national-book-awards-longlist-for-translated-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2018, \\\"Flights\\\" won the International Booker Prize, Britain's most important recognition for literature in translation, with the prize's chair, Lisa Appignanesi, heralding Tokarczuk as \\\"a writer of wonderful wit, imagination, and literary panache.\\\" Thanks to the Booker win, the author already had an eager readership ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2024/07/08/fitzcarraldo-editions-makes-challenging-literature-chic\"}],\"query\":\"Olga Tokarczuk Flights translated 25 languages International Booker Prize\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... Random House\\n\\nPajtim Statovci, \\\"Crossing\\\"\\n\\nTranslated by David Hackston\\n\\nPantheon Books / Penguin Random House\\n\\nOlga Tokarczuk, \\\"Drive Your Plow Over the Bones of the Dead\\\"\\n\\nTranslated by Antonia Lloyd-Jones\\n\\nRiverhead Books / Penguin Random House\\n\\nThe judges for the category this year are Keith Gessen, a founding editor ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2019-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d60\",\"snippet\":\" ... However before she came to Brooklyn Public Library, I had the chance to interview her in the autumn 2010, when Olga Tokarczuk's book Primeval and Other Times was translated into English by Antonia Lloyd Jones. Tokarczuk was then invited by the New Literature from Europe Festival and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bklynlibrary.org/blog/2020/01/12/olga-tokarczuk-interview\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... During her life, Szymborska published more than 30 books of poetry in Polish, from which more than 10 were translated into English. Other translations included Bulgarian, Romanian, Slovakian, Czech, Hungarian, Hebrew, Danish, Italian, Swedish, and German languages. Szymborska was awarded several prizes, including the Goethe Prize (1991) and ... \",\"title\":\"https://researchinpoland.org/polish-nobel-prize-winners/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d62\",\"snippet\":\" ... and at the same time receiving these very long passages of [Tokarczuk's] \\\"Flights\\\" and responding with passages of my own. So we courted each other with our projects.\\n\\nTranslation involves inhabiting someone else's language and work. But it's also a creative act.\\n\\nDralyuk: It's ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/books/story/2023-03-15/two-of-the-countrys-best-translators-are-married-and-competing-for-the-same-big-prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... Translated from the Spanish by Megan McDowell\\n\\nRiverhead Books / Penguin Random House\\n\\nSaša Stanišić, Where You Come From\\n\\nTranslated from the German by Damion Searls\\n\\nTin House Books\\n\\nYoko Tawada, Scattered All Over the Earth\\n\\nTranslated from the Japanese by Margaret Mitsutani\\n\\nNew Directions Publishing\\n\\nOlga Tokarczuk, The ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nationalbook.org/2022-national-book-awards-longlist-for-translated-literature/\"}],\"query\":\"Flights Olga Tokarczuk languages translated published year\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... Translated by Ottilie Mulzet\\n\\nNew Directions\\n\\nScholastique Mukasonga, \\\"The Barefoot Woman\\\"\\n\\nTranslated by Jordan Stump\\n\\nArchipelago Books\\n\\nYoko Ogawa, \\\"The Memory Police\\\"\\n\\nTranslated by Stephen Snyder\\n\\nPantheon Books / Penguin Random House\\n\\nPajtim Statovci, \\\"Crossing\\\"\\n\\nTranslated by David Hackston\\n\\nPantheon Books / Penguin Random House\\n\\nOlga Tokarczuk, \\\"Drive Your Plow ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2019-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d6